    <string name="cloud_title">Copy to my Google account</string>
    <string name="cloud_possible">Off by default. If you turn it on, Android copies your garden to your Google account, encrypted with your phone’s lock code: neither Google nor Sillon can read it. To get it back on another phone, you will need to enter the old phone’s code. Turning this setting off does not delete a copy already sent: delete it from your Google account’s backup. The JSON export above remains the safest way to switch phones.</string>
    <string name="cloud_unavailable">Unavailable: first set a lock code, pattern or password for your screen. Without it, Android does not encrypt the copy and Sillon does not send it.</string>
